# Email: the "confirm your email" message and the password reset mails.
# MAIL_MAILER=log writes every message to storage/logs/laravel.log and sends nothing: until a real mail server is set up here, nobody has to confirm their email.
# Now, until the domain sfd.dj exists: send with Gmail. Turn on 2-step verification on the Google account, make an App password at
# https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords, put the Gmail address in MAIL_USERNAME and the 16 letters (no spaces) in MAIL_PASSWORD, then set
#   MAIL_MAILER=smtp  MAIL_HOST=smtp.gmail.com  MAIL_PORT=587  MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=<the same Gmail address> (Gmail only sends as you)
# Later, from info@sfd.dj with Resend (resend.com): add the domain sfd.dj there, put the DNS records it shows at the domain, make an API key with
# "Sending access", then set
#   MAIL_MAILER=smtp  MAIL_HOST=smtp.resend.com  MAIL_PORT=587  MAIL_USERNAME=resend  MAIL_PASSWORD=<the API key, re_...>  MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=info@sfd.dj
# Then open Admin panel > Email and press "Send a test email to me".
MAIL_MAILER=log
MAIL_SCHEME=null
MAIL_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
MAIL_PORT=587
MAIL_USERNAME=null
MAIL_PASSWORD=null
MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS="info@sfd.dj"
MAIL_FROM_NAME="${APP_NAME}"

